# The assessment of AGT-007 against this build. The requirement identifier is this
# file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the identity
# is a second place for it to be wrong -- the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a record
# registration, and CHK-003.assessment states for this registry.
#
# AGT-007: "Nomos shall expose a read-only PrepareChangeContext operation through API, CLI,
# MCP, and capable clients. Given a pinned repository snapshot plus a symbol, selected
# scope, or task description, it shall combine KnowledgeWorkbench architecture context,
# claims, design decisions, examples, contradictions, and historical evidence with
# Nomos-resolved applicability, permitted scope, required verification, prohibited actions,
# evidence gaps, approved capabilities, and task-envelope inputs."
#
# No operation named or shaped like PrepareChangeContext exists anywhere -- a repo-wide
# search returns zero hits, and `nomos-api` (the one crate that projects orchestration seams
# to a second caller) exposes only `Handle_Gate_Run`/`Handle_Gate_Plan`/`Handle_Gate_Explain`,
# none of which take a symbol/scope/task description and return a combined context bundle.
#
# Several of the seven named "Nomos-resolved" ingredients are real and separately
# assessable: 'permitted scope' maps to `Territory`, the real, tested unit of
# mutual-exclusion scope a claimed item is bound to; 'required verification' maps to
# `LedgerItem`'s own `VerificationPredicate` field, distinct from the prose `done_when`;
# 'approved capabilities' has a real analog in `nomos_capability::Registry`. 'Task-envelope
# inputs' now has a real site too: `TaskEnvelope` (`nomos-agent-contracts`, since
# P13-AGT-001-002-TASK-ENVELOPE-WORK-RESULT) is exactly that -- a real, tested type
# genuinely constructed by `nomos-cli`'s `agent execute`/`agent judge-role` verbs before
# real agent work, confirmed Met against `AGT-001`. 'Prohibited actions' still has no real
# grounding beyond the same type's own `prohibited_changes` field, which nothing yet
# enforces (`P42-AGENT-ENVELOPE-ENFORCEMENT`). The KWB half (architecture context, claims,
# decisions, examples, contradictions, historical evidence) is unreachable:
# `KnowledgeReferenceId` exists (D-137) but, by that record's own text, "nothing yet
# produces or consumes one." Even if every ingredient existed, nothing stitches them into
# one operation exposed via CLI/API/MCP together -- `nomos-api` explicitly declines MCP.
verdict: Partial
site: crates/substrate/nomos-scope-verification/src/territory.rs#Territory
site: crates/substrate/nomos-ledger/src/item/ledger_item.rs#LedgerItem
site: crates/substrate/nomos-capability/src/registry.rs#Registry
site: crates/agent/nomos-agent-contracts/src/task_envelope.rs#TaskEnvelope
gap: crates/host/nomos-api/src/lib.rs#Handle_Gate_Run
gap: crates/contracts/nomos-contracts/src/digest128.rs#KnowledgeReferenceId
